Why was WebAssembly created?

JavaScript is powerful but has limitations.

Problems:

CPU-intensive tasks become slow.
Large calculations affect UI responsiveness.
Games and video editing applications need more performance.
Existing C/C++ applications could not directly run in browsers.

Example:

Imagine building:

Photoshop in browser
3D games
CAD software
Video editors

JavaScript alone may struggle.

So browsers introduced WebAssembly.

Goal:

"Bring desktop-level performance to the web."